# Docker build context exclusions for the NSE rotation research lab.
#
# The build context is the repository root, so this file is REPO-ROOT/.dockerignore.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data: never baked into an image. The DuckDB catalog + parquet reach the
# container through the ../data:/app/data bind mount in docker/compose.yaml.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
**/*.parquet
**/*.zip
# PDFs are proprietary/documented source material and are fetched, not shipped.
**/*.pdf
verification/
**/.cache/
**/*.duckdb
**/*.duckdb.wal

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal-only research artefacts. The public image ships the 124-column public
# CSVs only; the *.internal.csv files carry the internal gate vocabulary (130
# columns) and are gitignored. Keep them out of the build context (the
# Dockerfile additionally asserts their absence, so a regression fails the
# build rather than leaking them into a published image).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/*.internal.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VCS, virtualenvs, caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling / IDE / OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.github/
docker/
.python-version
.editorconfig
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Things that exist locally but are not part of the published image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch/TEMP trees (uv caches, pytest tmp dirs) are never image content.
.tmp/
scratch/
# NOTE: tests/ is NOT excluded here. The Dockerfile's `test` stage copies it, so
# the containerised pytest lane (`--profile test` / `--profile cli`) works
# without a bind mount. The published `runtime` stage never copies tests/.
pytest-cache-files-*/
.export-manifest.json
*.log
*.tmp
*.ipynb_checkpoints/
